<title>JAPAN: Moody's assigns Aa1 to Kyushu Electric eurobonds.</title>
<headline>Moody's assigns Aa1 to Kyushu Electric eurobonds.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moody's Investors Service said on Friday it had assigned its Aa1 rating to Kyushu Electric Power Co Inc's $300 million, 6.5 percent Eurobond offering due in 2001.</p>
<p>The rating was based on Kyushu Electric Power's importance to the local economy, its crucial role as a supplier within the Japanese utility industry, and its very favourable industry operating environment, it said.</p>
</text>
